.TH "LIBPKGEXEC" "3" "" "libpkgexec" "Version 2.1.1"
.SH NAME
libpkgexec \- native sealed program\-execution authority
.SH SYNOPSIS
\f[B]#include <libpkgexec/libpkgexec.h>\f[R]
.SH DESCRIPTION
\f[B]libpkgexec\f[R] defines immutable execution requests, call\-scoped resource admission, request\-bound cancellation control, backend capability profiles, and sealed execution evidence for exact \f[B]libpkgsource\f[R] program values.
It also provides a versioned codec for execution\-owned result evidence under caller\-supplied request and backend authorities.
.PP
The core performs no process, namespace, mount, cgroup, or filesystem syscalls.
Concrete executors implement \f[B]execution_backend\f[R] and must refuse requests whose required guarantees they cannot establish.
.SH BOUNDARY
The library does not acquire sources, materialize package inputs, build package artifacts, execute package lifecycle policy, apply filesystem transitions, or publish installed state.
.SH ERRORS
Contract failures throw \f[B]pkgexec::error\f[R].
Branch on \f[B]error_code\f[R], not diagnostic text.
.SH SEE ALSO
\f[B]pkgexec_request\f[R](3), \f[B]pkgexec_control\f[R](3), \f[B]pkgexec_result\f[R](3), \f[B]pkgexec_result_codec\f[R](3), \f[B]pkgexec_backend\f[R](3), \f[B]pkgexec_semantics\f[R](7), \f[B]libpkgsource\f[R](3)
